  <h2>Why a Regular Real Estate Sale Won't Work Right Now</h2>
  <p>When you list through a traditional agent, you're looking at 30-60 days minimum on the market. Then another 14-21 days to closing. By the time money hits your account, you're 90+ days out — and you might lose the deal to an appraisal issue or a buyer's inspection. If your mortgage is due in 30 days, that timeline doesn't exist for you.</p>
  <p>A cash buyer doesn't have those delays built in. No bank approval. No appraisal. No inspector finding deferred maintenance. We close when we say we close.</p>

  <h2>What Happens During a Cash Sale</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We evaluate the property and make you an offer within 24 hours</li>
    <li>You accept or counter — no middlemen, just direct negotiation</li>
    <li>We open escrow with a local Wichita title company</li>
    <li>Title company orders a title search and coordinates with any existing lieholders</li>
    <li>We close in 7-14 days, and you have cash in your account</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The Trade-Off Is Worth It When Time Matters</h2>
  <p>A cash offer will typically be below full retail market value. That's the price of speed and certainty. But run the math: a 5-6% agent commission, plus 60+ days of carrying costs (mortgage, utilities, insurance, property tax), plus the risk of the deal falling through entirely — and a cash offer often nets you more money in less time with way less stress.</p>
  <p>If you've got time to list and wait, traditional might win. If you've got a deadline, cash is the right move.</p>

